.TH "RTCERROR.RTCERROR" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCError.RTCError \- RTCError: RTCError() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]RTCError()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates and returns a
new \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] object instance.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new RTCError(options)
new RTCError(options, message)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R]
An object providing the details of the specific error in an
\f[CR]RTCErrorEvent\f[R].
The object has the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]errorDetail\f[R]
A string specifying the WebRTC\-specific error code identifying the type
of error that occurred.
This will be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]data\-channel\-failure\f[R]
The connection\(cqs \f[CR]RTCDataChannel\f[R] has failed.
.TP
\f[B]dtls\-failure\f[R]
The negotiation of the DTLS connection failed, or the connection was
terminated with a fatal error.
The error\(cqs \f[CR]message\f[R] contains details about the nature of
the error.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
If a fatal error is \f[I]received\f[R], set \f[CR]receivedAlert\f[R] to
the value of the received DTLS alert.
.IP \(bu 2
If a fatal error was \f[I]sent\f[R], set \f[CR]sentAlert\f[R] to the
alert\(cqs value.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]fingerprint\-failure\f[R]
The remote certificate for the \f[CR]RTCDtlsTransport\f[R] didn\(cqt
match any of the fingerprints listed in the SDP message.
If the remote peer can\(cqt match the local certificate against the
provided fingerprints, this error doesn\(cqt occur, though this
situation may result instead in a \f[CR]dtls\-failure\f[R] error.
.TP
\f[B]hardware\-encoder\-error\f[R]
The hardware encoder doesn\(cqt support the given configuration
parameters.
.TP
\f[B]hardware\-encoder\-not\-available\f[R]
The hardware encoder resources required to accomplish the requested
operation aren\(cqt available.
.TP
\f[B]sctp\-failure\f[R]
The SCTP negotiation has failed, or the connection has terminated with a
fatal error.
The SCTP cause code should be set in \f[CR]sctpCauseCode\f[R].
SCTP error cause codes 1\-13 are defined in the SCTP specification: RFC
4960, section 3.3.10.
.TP
\f[B]sdp\-syntax\-error\f[R]
The SDP syntax is invalid.
The SDP message line number at which the error was detected should be
set in \f[CR]sdpLineNumber\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]receivedAlert\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A positive integer value indicating a fatal DTLS error that was received
from the network.
Only set if the \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] string is
\f[CR]dtls\-failure\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]sctpCauseCode\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer specifying the SCTP cause code that indicates the cause of
the failed SCTP negotiation.
This should only be set if \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] is
\f[CR]sctp\-failure\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]sdpLineNumber\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer identifying the SDP message line number at which a syntax
error occurred.
Only set if \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] is \f[CR]sdp\-syntax\-error\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]sentAlert\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A positive integer indicating a fatal DTLS error that was sent out by
this device.
Only set if \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] is \f[CR]dtls\-failure\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]message\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string for the error message.
Defaults to the empty string (\f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]).
.SS Return value
A newly\-created \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] object instance.
.SH USAGE NOTES
This constructor does not do complete validation of the specified
\f[CR]candidateInfo\f[R] object or string.
